" administrere denne gruppe."

#. (itstool) path: varlistentry/term
#: admin_guide.xml:1799
msgid "Guests"
msgstr "Gæster"

#. (itstool) path: listitem/para
#: admin_guide.xml:1800
msgid ""
"Guests are visitors to your board who aren't logged in. You can limit what "
"guests can do by managing this usergroup."
msgstr ""
"Gæster er besøgende på dit board, der ikke er logget ind. Du kan begrænse "
"hvad gæster kan gøre ved at administrere denne brugergruppe."

#. (itstool) path: varlistentry/term
#: admin_guide.xml:1804
msgid "Registered Users"
msgstr "Tilmeldte brugere"

#. (itstool) path: listitem/para
#: admin_guide.xml:1805
msgid ""
"Registered users are a big part of your board. Registered users have already"
" registered on your board. To control what registered users can do, manage "
"this usergroup."
msgstr ""
"Tilmeldte brugere udgør en stor del af dit board. Tilmeldte brugere har "
"allerede tilmeldt sig dit board. For at styre hvad tilmeldte brugere kan "
"gøre, administrér denne brugergruppe."

#. (itstool) path: varlistentry/term
#: admin_guide.xml:1809
msgid "Registered COPPA Users"
msgstr "Tilmeldte COPPA-brugere"

#. (itstool) path: listitem/para
#: admin_guide.xml:1810
msgid ""
"Registered COPPA users are basically the same as registered users, except "
"that they fall under the <acronym>COPPA</acronym>, or Child Online Privacy "
"Protection Act, law, meaning that they are under the age of 13 in the U.S.A."
" Managing the permissions this usergroup has is important in protecting "
"these users. <acronym>COPPA</acronym> doesn't apply to users living outside "
"of the U.S.A. and can be disabled altogether."
msgstr ""
"Tilmeldte COPPA-brugere er grundlæggende det samme som tilmeldte brugere, "
"bortset fra at de falder under <acronym>COPPA</acronym>, eller Child Online "
"Privacy Protection Act, hvilket betyder at de er under 13 år i USA. "
"Administration af tilladelser for denne brugergruppe er vigtig for at "
"beskytte disse brugere. <acronym>COPPA</acronym> gælder ikke for brugere "
"bosat uden for USA og kan deaktiveres helt."

#. (itstool) path: listitem/para
#: admin_guide.xml:1780
msgid ""
"These are groups that are available by default in phpBB 3.3. You "
"<emphasis>cannot</emphasis> delete them, as the board needs them for various"
" features. You can still change their attributes (description, colour, rank,"
" avatar, and so forth) and group leaders. Users that register to your board "
"are automatically added to the predefined group \"Registered Users\", for "
"instance. Do not try to remove them manually through the database, or your "
"board will no longer function properly. <_:variablelist-1/>"
msgstr ""
"Dette er grupper, der er tilgængelige som standard i phpBB 3.3. Du "
"<emphasis>kan ikke</emphasis> slette dem, da boardet har brug for dem til "
"forskellige funktioner. Du kan stadig ændre deres egenskaber (beskrivelse, "
"farve, rang, avatar osv.) og gruppeledere. Brugere, der tilmelder sig dit "
"board, tilføjes f.eks. automatisk til den foruddefinerede gruppe \"Tilmeldte"
" brugere\". Forsøg ikke at fjerne dem manuelt via databasen, ellers vil dit "
"board ikke længere fungere korrekt. <_:variablelist-1/>"

#. (itstool) path: varlistentry/term
#: admin_guide.xml:1818
msgid "User defined groups"
msgstr "Brugerdefinerede grupper"

#. (itstool) path: listitem/para
#: admin_guide.xml:1820
msgid ""
"The groups you create by yourself are called \"User defined groups\". These "
"groups are similar to groups in 2.0. You may create as many as you want, "
